        "title": "Hamiltonian Mechanics and Phase Space",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Hamiltonian mechanics transforms Lagrangian mechanics via a **Legendre transform**, replacing\nvelocities q̇ with momenta p. The result is a 2n-dimensional phase space with a remarkably\nsymmetric structure that reveals the deep geometry of dynamics."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-HAMILTONIAN-MECHANICS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-HAMILTONIAN-MECHANICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:variational-calculus:05-hamiltonian-mechanics, git-history:variational-calculus:05-hamiltonian-mechanics]",
        "canonical_path": "variational-calculus/05-HAMILTONIAN-MECHANICS.md",
        "concepts": "[hamiltonian, mechanics]",
        "current_path": "variational-calculus/05-HAMILTONIAN-MECHANICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:variational-calculus:hamiltonian-mechanics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "variational-calculus",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[hamiltonian, mechanics]",
        "section": "variational-calculus",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Hamiltonian Mechanics and Phase Space",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|              LAGRANGIAN vs. HAMILTONIAN                               |\n|                                                                       |\n|  LAGRANGIAN           HAMILTONIAN                                     |\n|  -----------          -----------                                     |\n|  State: (q, q̇)       State: (q, p)  [phase space]                     |\n|  n 2nd-order ODEs     2n 1st-order ODEs                               |\n|  L = T − V            H = T + V  (usually energy)                     |\n|  q̈ = f(q, q̇)         q̇ = ∂H/∂p,  ṗ = −∂H/∂q                      |\n|  Tangent bundle TQ    Cotangent bundle T*Q                            |\n|                                                                       |\n|  ADVANTAGES OF HAMILTONIAN:                                           |\n|  • Phase space geometry (symplectic structure)                        |\n|  • Conservation: {H, f} = 0 ↔ f is conserved                          |\n|  • Canonical transformations simplify problems                        |\n|  • Direct path to quantum mechanics                                   |\n|  • Statistical mechanics (Liouville's theorem)                        |\n|                                                                       |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
